  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe #4107 snap in `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/iso.rs` is now decided per sample, not per edge:\n\n- `marching` reads each sample through a new `on_surface(v, step)`: a value within `NODE_SNAP * step` of zero (1e-6 of the step; 0.25 nm at a 0.25 mm step) reads +0.0, on the surface and on the outside of `d < 0`. One value per sample, so every tetrahedron that shares the sample reads the same one.\n- `tet`'s crossing returns the sample itself when one end reads exactly zero. The per-edge test `|da| < NODE_SNAP * |da - db|` is removed. An edge is crossed only from an inside end, so at most one end reads zero.\n\nWhy (from the issue): on a cut floor that lies on the lattice, the samples read about +-1e-12 with both signs. Decided per edge, two such samples of opposite sign each took the corners of their long edges, while the edge between them (both values tiny, so a moderate ratio) kept its crossing mid-edge. The facet through those three corners lay on one lattice edge, its normal was exactly zero, `push` dropped it, and the mesh opened by three edges per dropped facet.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/4180-snap-per-sample.md` (one PR, one file: #4107's file is not edited). #4107's decision listed \"a value within an epsilon of zero as zero\" under Considered and dropped; the new file says why it is the intent here.\n\n## Pinning test\n\nSynthetic shape only, in the existing `iso.rs` unit tests:\n- `a_floor_on_the_lattice_reading_both_signs_stays_closed`: a box on a 0.25 mm lattice (16 x 16 x 8 cells) whose top face is lattice layer 4, that layer read as +1e-12 or -1e-12 by `(i*7 + j*13) % 3`, every other sample the exact distance. Asserts the mesh is not empty, `open_edges == 0` and `unpaired_edges == 0`.\n  - On main `e6849c5ae` with only the test added: fails, `open_edges` left 45, right 0 (15 facets dropped).\n  - On this branch: passes, with the other 6 unit tests of `iso.rs`. #4107's `a_snapped_corner_is_the_sample_itself` is unchanged. Its either-end test calls `tet` directly, which no longer snaps, so it is renamed `an_edge_gets_the_same_corner_from_either_end_near_the_snap_threshold` and its comment says it now checks the interpolated corner from either end.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head `4d24dd119` (the review fix on `02a681e25`; base upstream/main `e6849c5ae`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 4 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 2.9 min. The gate map sends `sim::stock_sim::iso` to the sim unit tests, `stock_dual` and the app suite `stock_export`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: green, 6 steps (release build, `motion light: lib`, `adaptive_troch_island`, `adaptive_troch_neck`, `adaptive_troch_parallel`, `app light: pocket_pass_start`), 0 failed, 0 stalled, 39.3 min.\n- No heavy step: this is not a `P1` (work-issue section 3). No post or toolpath changed, so no example catalog suite.\n\nOn the first head `02a681e25`: quick green (4 steps, 0 failed: sim unit tests 280 passed, `stock_dual` 7, `stock_export` 2, 4.0 min) and clippy clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes.\n- The dual-contouring path: `extract_with` still serves the marching mesh only when the dual mesh fails its check; this change is in `marching` and `tet` only.\n- A sample just above the threshold on a floor of both signs: the threshold moves the case from \"both signs\" to \"one sign\" only for values under `NODE_SNAP * step`. Larger noise is not a snap case and is not pinned here.\n- In our own lane (outside this repository), cut stock meshes showed 24, 39 and 48 open edges after #4117, all multiples of three. Those meshes are not attached, and their recut with this change has not finished; the pin above is the evidence here.\n\nEffort: high (stock simulation is under the safety floor).\nChangelog: Stock simulation: a cut floor that lies on the sample lattice no longer opens the extracted mesh when its samples read tiny values of both signs.\n\nBranch: from upstream/main `e6849c5ae`; the diff is 2 files: `iso.rs` and `docs/decisions/4180-snap-per-sample.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4180\n",
